Fri Nov 13 23:41:53 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-window-placement.patch:
  * The programs started the help browser (XMayday) with
    -geom x<height>-20+50, i.e. at the right edge of the whole X
    screen (the far right of the second monitor). Dock it beside
    the main window that asked for help instead, with the same
    height: on the right, else on the left, narrower if needed,
    within that window's monitor (Xinerama) and work area. A
    running XMayday is moved there too (new GEOMETRY= remote
    command). The new -dock option only applies to the first
    window, so later XMayday windows are placed by the WM.
  * The launcher bar reopens where it was left, in its last
    layout (vertical/horizontal), "WM Activ" (shaped, without
    window manager) and "WM Buttons" modes, saved in
    ~/.axeneofficerc. A saved position off the monitors is reset
    to the centre of the pointer's monitor.
  * BuildRequires pkgconfig(xinerama).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 23:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-dialog-placement.patch: Motif centred each dialog
  over the place its parent had when the dialog was first created,
  and the file selectors and alerts are reused, so after the main
  window moved the Save dialog kept coming up elsewhere (alerts
  parented to the hidden shell appeared in the middle of the whole
  X screen, i.e. on the second monitor). Centre every dialog over
  its application window at each popup, or around the pointer when
  that window is not mapped.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 16:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-xquad-header-font.patch: XQuad drew the row and
  column headers (1, 2, 3...; A, B, C...) with its built-in Type 1
  rasterizer, which makes 1-bit glyphs with rudimentary hinting, so
  the digits and letters looked jagged at ~12 px. Draw them with the
  core X bitmap Helvetica (xorg-x11-fonts-legacy) closest to the
  zoomed size, like the rest of the UI, falling back to the old path
  when the server has none.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 05:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-lp64-drop-data.patch: the drag-and-drop of frames
  (XQuad, XAllWrite, Xclamation) sends the frame list pointer in two
  32-bit halves of a ClientMessage, and Xlib sign-extends each of
  them. The receiver added the halves back, so the pointer was wrong
  whenever bit 31 of the low half was set: dragging a rectangle to
  the trash (or moving it) crashed with SIGSEGV. Mask the low half

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 04:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-wm-close.patch: closing the main window of XQuad,
  XAllWrite or Xclamation, or an XMayday window, from the window
  manager destroyed it but left the process running without any
  window (and the AxeneOffice bar then only tried to raise that
  invisible instance). Run File > Quit (with its confirmation and
  save prompts) or File > Close instead

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 03:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add axene-office-launcher-close.patch: closing the AxeneOffice
  bar from the window manager destroyed its window but left the
  process running; quit on WM_DELETE_WINDOW
- Add axene-office-more-urw-fonts.patch: offer ITC Bookman,
  Palatino and ITC Zapf Chancery for documents, linked to their URW
  Type 1 clones from ghostscript-fonts-std

